{children:`channel_id`}),`), guilds (`,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`guild_id`}),`), and webhooks (`,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`webhook_id`}),` or `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`webhook_id + webhook_token`}),`). This means that an endpoint with two different top-level resources may calculate limits independently. As an example, if you exceeded a rate limit when calling one endpoint `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`/channels/1234`}),`, you could still call another similar endpoint like `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`/channels/9876`}),` without a problem.`]}),`\n`,_jsxs(_components.p,{children:[_jsx(_components.strong,{children:`Global rate limits`}),` apply to the total number of requests a bot or user makes, independent of any per-route limits. You can read more on `,_jsx(_components.a,{href:`/developers/topics/rate-limits#global-rate-limit`,children:`global rate limits`}),` below.`]}),`\n`,_jsx(Warning,{children:_jsxs(_components.p,{children:[_jsx(_components.a,{href:`/developers/resources/emoji#list-guild-emojis`,children:`Routes for controlling emojis`}),` do not follow the normal rate limit conventions. These routes are specifically limited on a per-guild basis to prevent abuse. This means that the quota returned by our APIs may be inaccurate, and you may encounter 429s.`]})}),`\n`,_jsx(Heading,{level:`2`,id:`header-format`,children:`Header Format`}),`\n`,_jsx(_components.p,{children:`For most API requests made, we return optional HTTP response headers containing the rate limit encountered during your request.`}),`\n`,_jsx(ManualAnchor,{id:`header-format-rate-limit-header-examples`}),`\n`,_jsx(_components.h6,{children:`Rate Limit Header Examples`}),`\n`,_jsx(CodeBlock,{numberOfLines:`6`,language:`text`,children:_jsx(_components.pre,{className:`shiki shiki-themes github-light-default dark-plus`,style:{backgroundColor:`#ffffff`,\"--shiki-dark-bg\":`#0B0C0E`,color:`#1f2328`,\"--shiki-dark\":`#D4D4D4`},language:`text`,children:_jsxs(_components.co